"1\n00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,229\nThe Learning Brain. Series 3: Generative AI\n\n2\n00:00:06,100 --> 00:00:07,331\nEpisode 10\n\n3\n00:00:07,411 --> 00:00:09,894\nCreativity and sameness\n\n4\n00:00:12,694 --> 00:00:15,116\nNearly three hundred people wrote a short,\n\n5\n00:00:15,136 --> 00:00:16,424\neight sentence story.\n\n6\n00:00:16,819 --> 00:00:18,322\nA third worked alone.\n\n7\n00:00:18,743 --> 00:00:21,913\nThe others could see one AI story idea,\n\n8\n00:00:22,086 --> 00:00:23,875\nor choose from up to five.\n\n9\n00:00:24,413 --> 00:00:26,285\nEveryone wrote their own story,\n\n10\n00:00:26,339 --> 00:00:28,598\nand none of them were professional writers.\n\n11\n00:00:28,768 --> 00:00:31,683\nSix hundred evaluators judged the stories.\n\n12\n00:00:32,081 --> 00:00:34,867\nWith access to five AI ideas,\n\n13\n00:00:35,082 --> 00:00:40,223\nstories were rated about eight percent more novel and nine percent more useful,\n\n14\n00:00:40,553 --> 00:00:43,474\nmeaning better crafted and closer to publishable.\n\n15\n00:00:43,644 --> 00:00:46,787\nThe biggest gains went to the least creative writers.\n\n16\n00:00:47,224 --> 00:00:48,944\nAI levelled the field,\n\n17\n00:00:49,223 --> 00:00:52,045\nas it did for the consultants in Episode three.\n\n18\n00:00:52,215 --> 00:00:53,336\nBut across the group,\n\n19\n00:00:53,448 --> 00:00:56,772\nthe AI assisted stories were more similar to each other.\n\n20\n00:00:57,103 --> 00:00:58,390\nEach writer gained.\n\n21\n00:00:58,830 --> 00:01:00,646\nThe collection lost variety.\n\n22\n00:01:01,039 --> 00:01:04,908\nThe AI ideas pulled writers toward similar stories.\n\n23\n00:01:05,078 --> 00:01:07,533\nThe authors call this a social dilemma.\n\n24\n00:01:07,955 --> 00:01:10,726\nEach person has a reason to use AI,\n\n25\n00:01:11,011 --> 00:01:13,890\nbut if everyone starts from the same suggestions,\n\n26\n00:01:14,090 --> 00:01:16,769\nthe shared pool of ideas narrows.\n\n27\n00:01:17,189 --> 00:01:19,507\nThe work drifts toward the same place.\n\n28\n00:01:19,677 --> 00:01:20,473\nA caution.\n\n29\n00:01:20,903 --> 00:01:24,250\nThese were short stories by non professional writers,\n\n30\n00:01:24,460 --> 00:01:26,695\nrated by online evaluators,\n\n31\n00:01:26,867 --> 00:01:28,900\nwith a model from twenty twenty three.\n\n32\n00:01:29,418 --> 00:01:32,969\nLonger, expert creative work may behave differently.\n\n33\n00:01:33,139 --> 00:01:33,897\nFor teaching.\n\n34\n00:01:34,261 --> 00:01:37,074\nHave students generate ideas alone first,\n\n35\n00:01:37,199 --> 00:01:40,125\nthen use AI to extend or challenge them.\n\n36\n00:01:40,567 --> 00:01:45,653\nReward difference: ask how a submission departs from what the AI suggested.\n\n37\n00:01:46,032 --> 00:01:47,090\nAnd in group work,\n\n38\n00:01:47,110 --> 00:01:48,898\ncompare ideas across the class,\n\n39\n00:01:48,918 --> 00:01:50,524\nto make sameness visible.\n\n40\n00:01:50,987 --> 00:01:55,032\nTreat the AI's first suggestion as the obvious answer to beat,\n\n41\n00:01:55,273 --> 00:01:56,756\nnot the one to use.\n\n42\n00:01:56,926 --> 00:01:59,664\nAI can lift each person's ideas.\n\n43\n00:01:59,938 --> 00:02:01,902\nKeeping them different is up to us.\n\n"
